Package: mscc-init-gui
Version: 1.0.12
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Multus SDR / MSCC Linux <local@localhost>
Depends: python3, python3-tk, python3-pyaudio
Recommends: python3-usb, mscc, pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio, alsa-utils
Homepage: https://local/mscc
Description: Graphical MSCC configuration wizard for Raspberry Pi OS
 Wizard GUI that writes $HOME/.local/mscc config (same files as CLI
 mscc-init): CAT/PTT, keyer, PROFICIO-MKII (ms-sdr PTT sense), operator
 audio (any rate; servers resample), fixed digi VirtualA / VirtualB.monitor.
 Sets ALSA levels to 100% and records card ids; mscc start re-applies
 via amixer (not .asoundrc).
 .
 Installs desktop menu entry "MSCC Init" under the MSCC category
 (same as Start/Stop/Status from the mscc package). Run as your
 normal user after package install (not during apt).
 .
 Requires a graphical session. For SSH-only use CLI mscc-init from
 the mscc package.
